aurora-latent-to-sm — third-party code
======================================

This repository contains and builds on third-party code.

1. Microsoft Aurora — MIT License
   - Copyright (c) Microsoft Corporation.
   - Source: https://github.com/microsoft/aurora  (pip: microsoft-aurora==1.7.0)
   - Used two ways:
       (a) as a pip dependency: models/*/train_hydr/ import from the `aurora`
           package (aurora.model.*, aurora.normalisation, aurora.batch);
       (b) models/*/train_hydr/aurora_lite.py is a modified copy of Aurora's
           model file (aurora/model/aurora.py). The MIT copyright header is
           retained; the only change is returning the decoder latent in
           forward(). The MIT License therefore applies to this file.

2. Aurora-Lite-Decoder (ETH Zürich) — GPL-3.0 License
   - F. Lehmann, F. Ozdemir, B. Soja, T. Hoefler, S. Mishra, S. Schemm,
     "Finetuning a Weather Foundation Model with Lightweight Decoders for
     Unseen Physical Processes", arXiv:2506.19088.
   - Source repository: https://github.com/lehmannfa/aurora-lite-decoder  (License: GPL-3.0)
   - The lightweight Perceiver decoder is taken from that repository:
       - models/mlp/train_hydr/decoder_lite.py   — copied verbatim from the
         upstream aurora/model/decoder_lite.py (ETH's original code, no MIT
         header).
       - models/mlp_enc/train_hydr/decoder.py,
         models/unet/train_hydr/decoder.py        — derived/modified from the
         same upstream decoder_lite.py.
     These files are therefore covered by GPL-3.0.

